# Mesh sources use .mpl, which Linguist assigns to JetBrains MPS — its only
# claimant, so the extension match short-circuits before any content is
# examined. That badges this repository as MPS and, because the MPS entry has
# `tm_scope: none`, renders every Mesh file as unhighlighted plain text.
#
# Linguist accepts only languages it already ships, so "Mesh" cannot be
# declared. Elixir is the closest structural match — it shares `do`/`end`
# blocks and `|>` pipes, which Rust's grammar would break on — so it restores
# highlighting at the cost of an inexact label.
*.mpl linguist-language=Elixir
